Subject: sd_register: disk controller modules register before sd's first open

30 section 2 patch 8 (S4-03), contract C4-1 section 3.  A root-class
disk controller registers each board from its _load:
sd_register(queuefn, c, base, name, rank).  The entry waits in the
core's table of four until sd's first open takes it (dlm_sd_close) and
ranks it with the floor's controllers; then registration is closed
(EBUSY).  The rank must be the class the module declares in .moddata
(rank=z3660, zorro, mobo or ide, now parsed); a fifth is ENOSPC.  A
_load that fails after registering leaves no entry: the backstop sweep
removes it.  The state harness covers each case.

